tors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. — *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. — *_FPAU Records which audience segments Google Analytics has assigned to you, used for reporting on visitor groups. — Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google Analytics FPAU Assigns a specific ID to the visitor. This allows the website to determine the number of specific user-visits for analysis and statistics. Session Google _gcl_au Used by Google AdSense for experimenting with advertisement efficiency across websites using their services. 3 months NID This cookies is used to collect website statistics and track conversion rates and Google ad personalisation 1 year Google Ads *__gcl_au Stores the identifier of the advert you clicked, so a later purchase or sign-up can be credited to the right campaign. — _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — DoubleClick/Google Marketing IDE This cookie is used for targeting, analyzing and optimisation of ad campaigns in DoubleClick/Google Marketing Suite 2 years LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Used by the social networking service, LinkedIn, for tracking the use of embedded services. 1 day bcookie Used by LinkedIn to track the use of embedded services. 1 year Facebook Facebook _fbp Used by Facebook to deliver a series of advertisement products such as real time bidding from third party advertisers 4 months Meta Meta Pixel *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
