    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/information-specialist-08-10-fte": {
      "title": "Information Specialist (0,8-1,0 fte)",
      "description": "Information Specialist (0,8-1,0 fte) | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Featured results Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Information Specialist (0,8-1,0 fte) Listen Published Tuesday 1 Sep 2026 Deadline Sunday 20 Sep 2026 Work area Research, development, innovation Organisational unit University Library (UB) Salary € 3.873 - € 5.264 Employment 0,8 fte - 1 fte Introduction As information specialist , you help students, lecturers, and researchers to find their way to the knowledge they need for studies or research in their field. You develop teaching materials and keep them updated, give online and offline workshops, and devise ways to optimise our services to even more closely meet the needs of our users. As part of a team consisting of other information specialists and a scholarly communication steward, you will have a solid and broad foundation in information literacy, but may also work on themes including responsible GenAI in education and (open) digital educational resources: topics that are in full development and have a direct impact on education and research. You are not necessarily expected to be an expert in all of these areas, particularly at the outset, however qualified candidates will have a reasonable level of foundational knowledge across these domains, as well as a willingness to learn, to adapt to emerging needs, and to support team colleagues where needed. Job description Examples of what your tasks may include (your own unique skills and experience in the area of information literacy may also play a role in your final task profile): Teaching information literacy to EUR students at both Bachelor’s and Master’s level Keep up with developments in the library world, information literacy, GenAI, and scientific information Developing the University Library’s information literacy training programmes, in terms of both content and format Supporting students in finding and using academic information sources, both on an individual basis and via workshops Participating in teaching projects and other supporting educational activities Contributing ideas on communicating about the UB and its services on social media Together with your team you report to the Team Leader Information Specialists. Every job is different, so in the beginning we will devote attention to your onboarding. If some of the work activities are new to you, we'll work together to figure out what you need, and draw up a development plan. Job requirements A completed higher professional education (HBO) or university (WO) degree Knowledge of how to search for and find academic information in relevant academic sources Experience in developing teaching materials and/or workshops Experience in and affinity with delivering online and offline teaching Experience in conducting literature reviews Excellent communication skills in Dutch and English (C1 level) Preferrable: Experience with and knowledge of responsible generative AI use Preferrable: Experience with and knowledge of open educational resources Competencies we will explore further during the interviews: Good communication skills Meticulous and analytical Service-oriented Innovative Employment conditions and benefits We offer you an internationally oriented and varied job in an enthusiastic team, with excellent working conditions in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities (CAO-NU). The start date of this position will be agreed is as soon as possible and you will be based at Campus Woudestein - Rotterdam at the University Library (UB). The salary is dependent on your experience and knowledge and ranges, for a fulltime appointment (38 hours per week), between €3.873 en €5.264 gross per month (scale 9), in accordance with the CAO-NU. The position is for 0,8-1,0 fte. The contract is offered for a period of 1 year and can be converted into an employment contract for an indefinite period if suitability is proven and if continued in the same position, if (financial and/or organizational) circumstances remain the same. Everything else we offer you; you can find below! - Everything you need for a good work-life balance : the option to work from home in consultation with your manager, 41 days of paid leave with a 40 hour contract, 8% holiday pay and an 8.3% end-of-year bonus, and a significant discount on a membership to our on-campus sports centre Opens external ! - Sustainable, inclusive and diverse work environment with an open culture, where you can be yourself and we care for each other and the world around us. Make the most of our bicycle budget, or join networks such as Young@EUR Opens external , FAME or QuEUR. - Time and space for your development in the broadest sense: development days and a personal career budget and free access to our university library . - Good pension with ABP , to which the EUR provides a 2/3 contribution, discounts on various collective insurances with Zilveren Kruis Achmea, Loyalis, and Allianz, and compensation for travel, working from home and home internet use. - Are you currently combining your job with parenthood, or do you want to do so in the future? EUR offers partially paid parental leave and fully paid additional birth leave for partners , and our campus features a daycare (daycare not paid for by EUR). - Moving to the Netherlands for your job with EUR? Then you may be eligible for the 30%-ruling if you meet the requirements of the Belastingdienst (Dutch tax agency), and with our Dual Career Programme we will also help your partner find the right job for them. Employer Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR) is an internationally oriented university with a strong social orientation in its education and research, as expressed in our mission ‘Creating positive societal impact’. EUR is home to 4.100 academics and professionals and almost 33.000 students from more than 140 countries. Everything we do, we do under the credo The Erasmian Way – Making Minds Matter. We’re global citizens, connecting, entrepreneurial, open-minded, and socially involved. These Erasmian Values function as our internal compass and create EUR’s distinctive and recognizable profile. From these values, with a broad perspective and with an eye for diversity, different backgrounds and opinions, our employees work closely together to solve societal challenges from the dynamic and cosmopolitan city of Rotterdam. Thanks to the high quality and positive societal impact of our research and education, EUR can compete with the top European universities. www.eur.nl . Faculty / Institute / Central service The University Library As the content manager of Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR), the University Library (UB) supports students, lecturers and researchers in creating, sharing and deepening knowledge. All services of the University Library are openly accessible. In this way, we contribute to a positive societal impact—not only within the academic community, but beyond it as well. The University Library has an open culture in which collaboration, working on the basis of trust, and taking responsibility are key values. Group The Library Education Support Department This department supports education at the university in the broadest sense. It consists of the Front Desk Team, the Information Specialists Team (of which you will be part), and two Faculty Liaisons. The department provides services in areas such as information literacy, the use of teaching materials within copyright regulations, responsible use of Generative AI, and the availability and use of open educational resources. The department works closely with colleagues from other teams and departments, both within and outside the University Library. Additional information Are you enthusiastic, but have questions about the position? Then you can contact Gina Kim, Team lead Information specialists via gina.kim@eur.nl . For questions about the procedure, you can contact our recruiter Iris Konijnendijk at iris.konijnendijk@eur.nl . Applying The University Library uses an anonymous application procedure . We attach great importance to diversity and believe it is essential that characteristics such as age, background and gender do not play any role in the selection process. How does the anonymous application procedure work? We kindly ask you to submit three documents: A CV containing only your initials A motivation letter containing only your initials A separate document containing your personal details Anonymising the CV and motivation letter means that names, age, gender (and any other personal identifying information) are omitted. After the initial selection, candidates are invited for an introductory interview. If this meeting is mutually positive, a second, more in-depth interview will follow, for which you will be asked to prepare a sample case. After the second interview, we will select the final candidate. Persons of all gender identities or expressions, sexual orientations, religions, ethnicities, ages, neurodiversities, functional impairments, citizenships, or any other aspect are welcome to apply and join the EUR community. We look forward to receiving your application! Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Job alert Please select your preferences. When a new job becomes available that matches these preference we'll send you an email. Fields marked with a * are required. First Name Last Name Email address Password Your password requires a minimum of 8 characters of which 2 non-alphabetic Confirm password Business Unit Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) Any Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) OK Cancel Expertise Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement Any Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement OK Cancel Share this page Interested? Apply now Applicant portal Open navigation for Information Specialist (0,8-1,0 fte) Close Interested? Apply now Interested? Apply now Compare 0 study programmes Close Compare 0 study programmes 0 of 3 study programmes selected. @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Information Specialist (0,8-1,0 fte) Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close Our website uses cookies Overview This website uses cookies and similar technologies (hereinafter collectively: 'cookies'). In this menu, you can choose which types of cookies and purposes you consent to. Functional: ​​These cookies are technically necessary for the website to function properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Acce